Here's an R function that checks if all non-NA elements in a character vector can be converted to numeric:

```R
is_all_numeric <- function(x) {
  x <- as.character(x) # Convert to character to handle NA values
  is.na(x) <- FALSE # Remove NA values from the character vector

  tryCatch(
    {
      as.numeric(x)
    },
    error = function(e) {
      return(FALSE)
    }
  )
}
```

To use this function, simply pass a character vector as an argument:

```R
x <- c("1", "2", "3", "4", "5", NA, "6")
if (is_all_numeric(x)) {
  print("All non-NA elements in x can be converted to numeric.")
} else {
  print("Not all non-NA elements in x can be converted to numeric.")
}
```

In this example, the output will be:

```
Not all non-NA elements in x can be converted to numeric.
```

The `tryCatch` function is used to handle any errors that may occur during the conversion process. If an error occurs, the function returns `FALSE`. Otherwise, it returns `TRUE`.

