Here's a simple React utility to remove widows. This component takes in a text prop and returns the text with any widows removed. A widow is a line that is separated from the rest of the paragraph by a line break.

```jsx
import React from 'react';

const RemoveWidows = ({ text }) => {
  const lines = text.split('\n');
  const lastLine = lines[lines.length - 1];

  if (lastLine.trim() === '') {
    lines.pop();
  }

  return (
    <div>
      {lines.join('\n')}
    </div>
  );
};

export default RemoveWidows;
```

To use this component, you can pass in a text prop like this:

```jsx
<RemoveWidows text="This is some sample text that may contain widows." />
```

This will render the text without any widows.

