To create a Socket for Chatroom using PHP, you can use the Socket extension. Here's an example of how to create a simple chatroom using PHP and Sockets:

1. First, make sure you have the Socket extension enabled in your PHP configuration. You can check this by running the following PHP code:
```php
<?php
phpinfo();
?>
```
Look for the "Socket" extension in the list of loaded extensions. If it's not enabled, you can enable it by editing your PHP configuration file (usually `php.ini`) and uncommenting the line that enables the Socket extension.

2. Next, create a PHP script to handle the chatroom functionality. Here's an example of how to do this:
```php
<?php
// Initialize the Socket
$socket = socket_create(AF_INET, SOCK_STREAM, SOL_TCP);
if ($socket === false) {
    die("Error creating socket: " . socket_strerror($socket));
}

// Bind the Socket to a port and IP address
$address = 'localhost';
$port = 12345;
socket_bind($socket, $address, $port);

// Listen for incoming connections
socket_listen($socket);

// Accept incoming connections
while (true) {
    $new_socket = socket_accept($socket);
    if ($new_socket === false) {
        continue;
    }

    // Handle incoming messages
    while (true) {
        $message = socket_read($new_socket, 1024);
        if ($message === false || $message == "") {
            break;
        }

        // Broadcast the message to all connected clients
        socket_write($new_socket, "Received: " . $message);
        socket_broadcast($socket, $message);
    }

    // Close the connection
    socket_close($new_socket);
}

// Close the Socket
socket_close($socket);
?>
```
